<Legal title="Refund and cancellation policy" description="How to cancel a paid FlutterProbe plan, what happens when you do, and when a payment is refunded." other="/reembolsos/">
  <p>This is a translation for your convenience. The <a href="/reembolsos/" hreflang="es">Spanish version</a> is the binding one, and it prevails if the two differ. This policy is part of the <a href="/terms/">terms of service</a>.</p>

  <h2>1. The Free plan and the free tools</h2>
  <p>The Free plan and the tools that run on your machine cost nothing, so there is nothing to cancel or refund. You can stop using them at any time.</p>

  <h2>2. How to cancel a paid plan</h2>
  <p>You can cancel at any time, with no penalty and without giving a reason, in either of these ways:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>online, in the billing portal; the link to it is in the emails we send about your subscription;</li>
    <li>by email to <a href="mailto:support@alphawavesystems.com">support@alphawavesystems.com</a> from the billing email address or from an account of the team, naming the team.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The cancellation takes effect on the charges at once: from that moment no further charge is made. We confirm it by email.</p>

  <h2>3. What happens after you cancel</h2>
  <p>The team keeps the paid plan until the end of the month already paid for, and then moves to the Free plan with its limits. Your data stays under the periods of the <a href="/privacy/">privacy notice</a>. You can subscribe again whenever you want.</p>

  <h2>4. Refunds</h2>
  <p>A paid plan is paid monthly in advance, and you can cancel before any renewal. For that reason a month that has started is not refunded, in whole or in part, when you cancel during it, except in the cases below.</p>
  <p>We refund a charge, in full or in the part that applies, when:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>you were charged twice for the same period;</li>
    <li>you were charged after your cancellation took effect;</li>
    <li>you were charged an amount different from the one shown to you, in which case we refund the difference, or there was any other billing error;</li>
    <li>we stop offering the services or your plan during a period you paid for, in which case we refund the part of the period that was not provided;</li>
    <li>the paid services were unavailable, for reasons attributable to us, for a substantial part of the paid period, in which case we refund or credit what the law requires.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>This policy does not limit any right to a refund, to cancel or to compensation that the law gives you and that cannot be waived, including consumer protection law where it applies to you.</p>

  <h2>5. How to ask for a refund</h2>
  <p>Write to <a href="mailto:support@alphawavesystems.com">support@alphawavesystems.com</a> with the billing email address, the date and the amount of the charge, and the reason. Please tell us within 60 days of the charge so that we can check it; this does not shorten any period the law gives you. We review every request and answer by email.</p>
  <p>An approved refund goes back to the payment method that was charged, in the currency of the charge. Your bank or card issuer decides when it appears on your statement and, if your account uses another currency, at what rate.</p>

  <h2>6. Disputes with your bank</h2>
  <p>If you see a charge you do not recognise, write to us first: we can usually resolve it faster than a dispute opened with the bank. Opening a dispute remains your right. While a dispute that covers the current period is open, we may suspend the paid features of the team.</p>

  <h2>7. Consumers in Mexico</h2>
  <p>If we cannot resolve your complaint, you may go to the Procuraduría Federal del Consumidor (PROFECO).</p>
</Legal>
